    "notes": "Antonio Stradivari, 1693, NMM 03598 — the \"Harrison\", one of the Long Pattern instruments. The record publishes back length 363, upper bout 161, centre 109 and lower 203 mm, and is internally consistent: scaled to the published 203 mm lower bout the top photograph measures 363.1 mm long. Height and lower bout width are the published figures; upper and centre bout are 161.8 and 109.2 read off the top photograph, which here agrees with the record more closely than the back does (162.7).\n\nBout radii, corner positions and the corner structure come from fitting the recipe solver to the right-hand silhouette at 9.8 px/mm: 0.34 mm mean deviation, the closest of the three traced in this pass, though the upper corner reaches 0.80 mm where the photograph shows structure behind the top plate's edge. Simple corners fitted best (0.331 mm) ahead of compound small arcs (0.346) and a compound straight run (0.423). The last is worth recording: a straight section into the corner is common in this period, and the variant is reachable on this instrument — it simply does not win on this silhouette. Right side only. No arching, no f-holes."
  },
